{
  "dataset_title": "SatNOGS 22 July 2026 bad-rated shift cohort with make-good candidates through 25 July, plus per-station operator availability declarations",
  "retrieved_at_utc": "2026-08-07T12:56:31.270Z",
  "license": "Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 (CC BY-SA 4.0) for the packaged normalized SatNOGS observation snapshot and derived lookup views.",
  "primary_documentation": "https://docs.satnogs.org/projects/satnogs-network/en/latest/api.html",
  "selection_rule": "The first 18 cursor pages of status=bad observations in the fixed collection envelope were de-duplicated by observation id; the selected 96 cases occur during the 22 July 17:20-23:58 UTC shift. Up to two cursor pages of status=good observations in the fixed recovery horizon were retrieved for frequent transmitter pairs. Acquisition URLs preserve the original query record, including an unsupported satellite__norad_cat_id parameter; exact NORAD catalog ID plus transmitter UUID were therefore post-filtered locally before inclusion and are not treated as server-side guarantees. Eighty cases with at least one compatible later contact were selected round-robin across repeated pairs, then sixteen cases without a compatible contact were added. The JSON files are normalized transformed snapshots rather than preserved raw API response pages; station, transmitter and TLE lookup views were derived from observation records.",
  "compatibility_rule": "Exercise policy: a candidate is compatible when it is a public status=good observation of the same NORAD catalog id and transmitter UUID, uses the same observation frequency, reports an active transmitter and max_altitude at least 10 degrees, starts after the bad-rated case ended, and starts within 72 hours of that end. A compatible candidate is only bookable if the owning station's availability declaration in station_operations/ permits it. The altitude, horizon, station-gating and optimization rules are exercise policy, not SatNOGS operating rules.",
